## Development and integration

Run the repository's `doctor` operation when the environment is in doubt. Follow the selected execution policy for required integration checks; local feedback may be available in every mode.

For bounded changes to a healthy gate map, use affected commands and mandatory invariants. Reuse durable setup/execution evidence only while recorded source/input, runtime, lockfile, service, platform and policy invariants remain unchanged and no drift is observed. Report reusable, invalidated and fresh evidence separately from assumptions; rerun invalidated checks. Deep risk still requires relevant full validation and release acceptance proves the exact candidate/artifact.

## Extended validation

Run `ci:extended` when the change affects higher-risk boundaries. Run `jobs:local` only when Docker/local isolation adds evidence such as services, platform parity, or disposable integration infrastructure.

